# Build output dirs
/build-android/
/build-appimage-local/
/build-ci/
/build-gha/
/build-local/
/builddir/
/dist/
/misrc_tools/build/

# /build/ used to hold tracked helper scripts alongside `cmake -B build` output, so
# the pattern here had to ignore the output while un-ignoring the helpers. Upstream
# 705a42b deleted the last of them (build-static.sh, install-udev-rules.sh,
# LEGAL.txt), so /build/ is now nothing but CMake output and a bare ignore is right.
# Restore the `/build/*` + `!` negations if a tracked helper ever lands here again.
/build/

# Python bytecode. misrc_tools/test/ci_guard_tests.py is importable as a module and
# not only runnable as a script, so anything that imports it (tooling, a REPL, another
# test) drops a __pycache__ next to the tests.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Vendored dependency build/install staging
/.deps/

# CI artifact output
/.ci-artifacts/

# Scratch
/.tmp/

# Android debug keystore (generated, never committed)
/android/debug.keystore
# Android Meson cross-file is auto-generated by android/gen-cross-file.sh with
# machine-specific NDK + DEPS_PREFIX paths. Never commit it (it dirty-tags the
# version string on any other host/CI). Run gen-cross-file.sh before meson.
/android/aarch64-linux-android.ini
# Android deps-versions.txt is auto-generated by android/build-deps-android.sh
# with a build timestamp + the host NDK path. Never commit it for the same
# reason: regenerating it on CI dirties the tree and tags the version -dirty.
/android/deps-versions.txt

# Claude worktrees are local scratch, never repo content
**/.claude/worktrees/

# clangd's background index. It persists parsed translation units as *.idx under
# .cache/clangd/index/ so a restart does not reindex the whole tree
# (https://clangd.llvm.org/design/indexing). Machine-local and regenerated on demand:
# never repo content, and large enough to be worth keeping out of git status. The **/
# prefix matters: a pattern with an embedded slash is anchored to this file's directory,
# so a bare .cache/clangd/ would miss an editor opened on a subdirectory project root.
**/.cache/clangd/

# macOS Finder/system droppings. Every pattern here is deliberately unanchored (no
# leading or embedded slash), which in gitignore means "match at any depth" -- these
# files appear in whatever directory Finder happened to touch, not just the root.
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.fseventsd
.Spotlight-V100
.TemporaryItems
.Trashes
.VolumeIcon.icns
.com.apple.timemachine.donotpresent

# Finder droppings specific to network shares and removable volumes
.AppleDB
.AppleDesktop
.apdisk
Network Trash Folder
Temporary Items

# Deliberately NOT ignored: the custom-folder-icon file, usually written `Icon?` in
# macOS ignore templates. The real artifact is "Icon" plus a literal CR, but `?` is a
# single-character glob, so `Icon?` also matches assets/Icons/ -- a tracked directory
# holding MISRC_Icon.png. Git does not descend into an ignored directory, so that
# pattern would silently hide anything added there. Custom folder icons are rare and
# only ever created by hand in Finder; the pattern is not worth the trap.

# macOS toolchain artifacts. There is no Xcode project in this repo -- meson is the only
# build system, and the macOS CI leg stages MISRC.app under $RUNNER_TEMP, outside the
# tree -- so these only fire if someone opens the sources in Xcode or leaves debug
# symbols outside one of the build-* dirs already ignored above.
*.dSYM/
DerivedData/
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
